None
The table structure information is (table names): 
['all_star', 'appearances', 'manager_award', 'player_award', 'manager_award_vote', 'player_award_vote', 'batting', 'batting_postseason', 'player_college', 'fielding', 'fielding_outfield', 'fielding_postseason', 'hall_of_fame', 'home_game', 'manager', 'manager_half', 'player', 'park', 'pitching', 'pitching_postseason', 'salary', 'college', 'postseason', 'team', 'team_franchise', 'team_half']
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant tables / columns and how they will probably be used  

• batting.g, batting.r, batting.h, batting.hr : season totals of Games‑played, Runs, Hits and Home‑Runs for every hitter.  
• batting.player_id / batting.year : needed for grouping or filtering by year or by player.  
• player.player_id  : joins the master table with “batting”.  
• player.name_given : the given (first & middle) names that the question asks for.  
Typical conditions to add  
• WHERE "g" IS NOT NULL  (or r, h, hr) – screen out blank rows.  
• HAVING MAX(..) – to keep only the record(s) that hold the highest value.  
• JOIN "player" USING ("player_id") – to attach the given names.  

Below are ten exploration queries that move from simple inspection to the complete answer.  
Each query is limited to 20 rows so they can run quickly while you explore.

```sql
-- 1. Peek at the four batting columns of interest
SELECT "player_id","year","g","r","h","hr"
FROM   "batting"
WHERE  "g" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 2. What is the single‑season record for Games played?
SELECT MAX("g") AS "max_games"
FROM   "batting"
WHERE  "g" IS NOT NULL;
```

```sql
-- 3. Which season(s) reach that Games‑played record?
SELECT "player_id","year","g"
FROM   "batting"
WHERE  "g" = (SELECT MAX("g") FROM "batting" WHERE "g" IS NOT NULL)
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Same result as #3, but with players’ given names
SELECT p."name_given", b."year", b."g"
FROM   "batting"  AS b
JOIN   "player"   AS p USING ("player_id")
WHERE  b."g" = (SELECT MAX("g") FROM "batting" WHERE "g" IS NOT NULL)
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Highest single‑season Runs total and the player(s) who achieved it
SELECT p."name_given", b."year", b."r" AS "runs"
FROM   "batting"  AS b
JOIN   "player"   AS p USING ("player_id")
WHERE  b."r" = (SELECT MAX("r") FROM "batting" WHERE "r" IS NOT NULL)
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Highest single‑season Hits total and the player(s) who achieved it
SELECT p."name_given", b."year", b."h" AS "hits"
FROM   "batting"  AS b
JOIN   "player"   AS p USING ("player_id")
WHERE  b."h" = (SELECT MAX("h") FROM "batting" WHERE "h" IS NOT NULL)
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Highest single‑season Home‑Run total and the player(s) who achieved it
SELECT p."name_given", b."year", b."hr" AS "home_runs"
FROM   "batting"  AS b
JOIN   "player"   AS p USING ("player_id")
WHERE  b."hr" = (SELECT MAX("hr") FROM "batting" WHERE "hr" IS NOT NULL)
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Union of the four leader lists so you can see them side by side
SELECT 'Games'      AS "category", p."name_given", b."year", b."g"  AS "value" FROM "batting" b JOIN "player" p USING("player_id")
WHERE b."g"  = (SELECT MAX("g")  FROM "batting" WHERE "g"  IS NOT NULL)
UNION ALL
SELECT 'Runs',       p."name_given", b."year", b."r"  FROM "batting" b JOIN "player" p USING("player_id")
WHERE b."r"  = (SELECT MAX("r")  FROM "batting" WHERE "r"  IS NOT NULL)
UNION ALL
SELECT 'Hits',       p."name_given", b."year", b."h"  FROM "batting" b JOIN "player" p USING("player_id")
WHERE b."h"  = (SELECT MAX("h")  FROM "batting" WHERE "h"  IS NOT NULL)
UNION ALL
SELECT 'HomeRuns',   p."name_given", b."year", b."hr" FROM "batting" b JOIN "player" p USING("player_id")
WHERE b."hr" = (SELECT MAX("hr") FROM "batting" WHERE "hr" IS NOT NULL)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Career totals (sum over all seasons) for every player,
--    showing the top 20 in Games, Runs, Hits or HR
SELECT p."name_given",
       SUM(b."g")  AS "career_games",
       SUM(b."r")  AS "career_runs",
       SUM(b."h")  AS "career_hits",
       SUM(b."hr") AS "career_hr"
FROM   "batting" b
JOIN   "player"  p USING ("player_id")
GROUP  BY p."player_id"
ORDER  BY "career_games" DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL: players who hold the single‑season record
--     in ANY of the four categories, with the actual record value
SELECT DISTINCT p."name_given",
       CASE
           WHEN b."g"  = (SELECT MAX("g")  FROM "batting" WHERE "g"  IS NOT NULL) THEN 'Games'      || ': ' || b."g"
           WHEN b."r"  = (SELECT MAX("r")  FROM "batting" WHERE "r"  IS NOT NULL) THEN 'Runs'       || ': ' || b."r"
           WHEN b."h"  = (SELECT MAX("h")  FROM "batting" WHERE "h"  IS NOT NULL) THEN 'Hits'       || ': ' || b."h"
           WHEN b."hr" = (SELECT MAX("hr") FROM "batting" WHERE "hr" IS NOT NULL) THEN 'HomeRuns'   || ': ' || b."hr"
       END AS "record_held"
FROM   "batting" b
JOIN   "player"  p USING ("player_id")
WHERE  b."g"  = (SELECT MAX("g")  FROM "batting" WHERE "g"  IS NOT NULL)
    OR b."r"  = (SELECT MAX("r")  FROM "batting" WHERE "r"  IS NOT NULL)
    OR b."h"  = (SELECT MAX("h")  FROM "batting" WHERE "h"  IS NOT NULL)
    OR b."hr" = (SELECT MAX("hr") FROM "batting" WHERE "hr" IS NOT NULL)
LIMIT  20;
```

